@startuml testing
title How the plugin is tested with trmnlp test

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor Developer as dev
participant "test.sh\n(trmnl/trmnlp image + zbar)" as cli
participant "plugin/tests/payment_qr_spec.rb\n(RSpec, trmnlp test)" as spec
participant "trmnlp\n(its own Liquid, settings\nand stored webhook data)" as harness
participant "shared.liquid\n(data + layout)" as liquid
participant "Firefox page\n(device classes, palette,\nframework + fonts)" as page
participant "zbar" as zbar

dev -> cli : ./test.sh [-e filter]
cli -> cli : trmnlp lint
cli -> spec : trmnlp test --report: 146 tests
loop every test
  opt CR LF test
    spec -> spec : copy plugin/, give shared.liquid CR LF\nline endings as TRMNL's web editor preview did
  end
  spec -> harness : render(device:, view:, orientation:, dark_mode:,\nvariables:, custom_fields:, data:)
  harness -> liquid : render with the settings and the webhook "payment"
  liquid --> harness : markup
  harness -> page : open at the device's size
  page --> spec : screen
  spec -> page : locators and geometry
  note right of spec
    layout chosen = expected (rule written in the test)
    no overflow, nothing on the QR, quiet zone >= 6 px,
    QR modules >= 2 px, code fills >= 98 % of its box
    price rows right-aligned and full width, list marks,
    dividers, captions per language, title bar
  end note
  spec -> zbar : picture reduced to the device's bit depth
  zbar --> spec : exact QR payload (also in dark mode)
end
cli --> dev : "146 examples, 0 failures" + report (report/index.html)

== Ship ==
dev -> dev : trmnlp push, then trmnlp pull
note right of dev
  the device is the last check: when the server shows
  something trmnlp does not, that difference becomes a
  new test on a patched copy of the template
end note
@enduml
